0..78 Comment "// Eliminating the circle: a case over it reads its point, and the loop at the"
79..155 Comment "// point is owed. A dependent case carries its answer at the point along the"
156..233 Comment "// loop back to itself, by conversion, or supplies that path as a loop arm; a"
234..310 Comment "// non-dependent case maps the loop to reflexivity unless a loop arm chooses"
311..389 Comment "// its image. Transport along a word computes as the book\'s § 2.11 states it:"
390..463 Comment "// in a family of paths it composes on the side the endpoint varies, in a"
464..536 Comment "// constant family it is the identity, and in a family running its point"
537..627 Comment "// through a map it is the map\'s image of the word. `Path.step`, `Path.back` and `Path.ap`"
628..703 Comment "// stand bare where no path type is written: each reads its path\'s type off"
704..728 Comment "// the words it acts on."
730..808 Comment "// The circle, the integers, every point\'s loop and reflexivity, and the flip."
809..815 Keyword "import"
816..817 StringLit "\""
